title: 'Gnomon on Windows: W0 test fixes, P03, Rust helper, kernel on a named pipe, sandbox design validated'
summary: Took over the Windows parity pass on the founder's Windows machine (branch feat/gnomon-windows off feat/gnomon). Fixed the Windows CI test failures (CRLF shebang, 8.3 temp paths, POSIX fixtures), ran probe P03, built the Rust platform helper (pipe/home DACLs, job launcher, durable rename, boot id, ShellExecute), moved the kernel onto an owner-only named pipe with an owner-only home, and validated the W5 session-sandbox design (restricted token + session-SID deny ACEs + Low integrity + private Low desktop + job UI limits) with Claude Code running under it. Aegis approve-with-fixes, all Medium/Low fixes folded in. `gnomon dev init` and `dev up` now run on Windows.
symbols_touched:
  - '#gnomon-helper'
  - '#gnomon-helper-win32'
  - '#gnomon-kernel'
  - '#socket'
  - $daemon-lifecycle
  - '#identity'
  - '#gnomon-probes'
